Subject: phy: qcom: qmp-ufs: reset the SM8550 PCS before calibration

The Kalama UFS PHY driver in Samsung's kernel writes UFS_PHY_SW_RESET = 1
before the calibration tables, on the SM-X710 and the SM-X910 alike (the
two kernels carry the same phy-qcom-ufs-qmp-v4-kalama.c).  Mainline never
asserts the PCS reset of a PHY that has one: qmp_ufs_phy_init() returns
before taking the external reset, and calibrate only clears SW_RESET and
sets SERDES_START.  Nothing else writes either bit, so once the first
calibration has run, both writes change nothing on a PCS that kept its
registers.

Without it a resume ended in a PCS_READY timeout on both boards: the
SM-X910 in a pm_test=devices cycle and in a deep suspend on 2026-09-09
(kernel #8); the SM-X710 in its first deep sleep since rpmhpd syncs at
boot, on 2026-11-21 (Type-C kit revision 7), where all 15 recalibrations
of the UFS host's reset and restore timed out and the root went read-only.
The SM-X910 has carried this assertion since kernel #10, through its
RAM-root and normal-root deep cycles.  That the missing assertion caused
the timeouts is probable, not proven.

Assert it for every SM8550 PHY, without a board check: the PHY, its tables
and the stock sequence are the same on both tablets.  Nothing changes at
run time on the SM-X910, which already ran this write; its compiled
calibration loses only the of_machine_is_compatible() call.
qphy_setbits() reads the register back before the tables go in.

--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-ufs.c
@@ -1990,6 +1990,19 @@ static int qmp_ufs_phy_calibrate(struct
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	/*
+	 * SM8550: assert the PCS reset before the calibration tables, as the
+	 * Kalama driver in Samsung's kernel does on the SM-X710 and the
+	 * SM-X910 alike.  Nothing else asserts it after the first
+	 * calibration, so on a PCS that kept its registers through a power
+	 * collapse (its GDSC has RETAIN_FF_ENABLE) the clear and SERDES_START
+	 * below change nothing.  That is the probable cause of the PCS_READY
+	 * timeouts that ended a resume on both tablets.  qphy_setbits() reads
+	 * the register back before the tables go in.
+	 */
+	if (cfg == &sm8550_ufsphy_cfg && !cfg->no_pcs_sw_reset)
+		qphy_setbits(pcs, cfg->regs[QPHY_SW_RESET], SW_RESET);
+
 	qmp_ufs_init_registers(qmp, cfg);
 
 	ret = reset_control_deassert(qmp->ufs_reset);
